// Title: Time Machine Backup Disabled Via Tmutil - MacOS
// Sigma ID: 2c95fa8a-8b8d-4787-afce-7117ceb8e3da
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Pratinav Chandra
// Date: 2024-05-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: impact, T1490
// Description: Detects disabling of Time Machine (Apple's automated backup utility software) via the native
//   macOS backup utility "tmutil". An attacker can use this to prevent backups from occurring.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administrator activity
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/master/atomics/T1490/T1490.md#atomic-test-12---disable-time-machine
//   - https://www.loobins.io/binaries/tmutil/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_tmutil_disable_backup.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "/tmutil" or ProcessCommandLine contains "tmutil") and ProcessCommandLine contains "disable"
